# Java service pattern

- Java 21. Constructor injection. No Lombok, field injection, or `javax.*` imports.
- Controllers return `ResponseEntity<ApiResponse<T>>` and stay thin. Business rules live in `service` or `domain`.
- Request bodies are validated records. Entities stay package-private to JPA and are never returned directly.
- Throw `ApexException` with an `ErrorCode`. Do not catch and drop exceptions.
- Repositories use explicit `@Query` when the method name would hide a join or a lock.
- Kafka payloads are JSON objects inside `EventEnvelope`. Consumers are idempotent.
- Tests are plain JUnit for domain rules. Do not boot PostgreSQL, Kafka, or Eureka in unit tests.

```java
// GOOD
return ResponseEntity.ok(ApiResponse.ok(mapper.toResponse(order)));

// BAD
return orderRepository.findAll();
```
